Title:
voidsyscall — Cross-platform syscall-powered implant & C2 (Zero WinAPI)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- voidsyscall is an offensive implant framework and C2 where Windows functionality is implemented via direct/indirect NT syscalls resolved at runtime from the in-memory ntdll export table, avoiding WinAPI imports and common usermode hooks.  
- It targets EDR usermode monitoring by using Plan9 assembly syscall stubs, hashed API names (djb2), SSN (syscall number) resolution via prologue scanning (including Hell’s Gate-style patterns), and an ntdll “unhook” routine that restores .text from disk-mapped bytes.  
- The agent supports multiple C2 transports (HTTPS, DNS TXT, ICMPv4) with AES-256-GCM per-message encryption and a tasking protocol for shell, injection, patching, evasion, token ops, and more.  
- It includes four rotating injection techniques (section mapping, process hollowing, APC queuing, module stomping), plus anti-analysis checks (VM/sandbox/debugger/timing) and optional auto-destruct behavior.  
- Additional capabilities cover registry Run-key persistence, token manipulation/impersonation, VAD enumeration/hide, handle enumeration and “EDR handle” closure, and memory/stack encryption utilities.  
- Useful primarily for red teams, implant developers, and security researchers studying syscall-based tradecraft and usermode EDR bypass patterns.

Technical Focus:
- Runtime syscall number (SSN) resolution via PEB/LDR + PE export parsing + prologue scanning
- Direct vs indirect syscalls (syscall;ret gadget) and Plan9 assembly stubs in Go
- Usermode unhooking of ntdll (.text restore) and syscall cache/fingerprinting
- Process injection tradecraft (section mapping, hollowing, APC, module stomping)
- Evasion patches (AMSI/ETW/NtTraceEvent/DbgUiRemoteBreakin/Instrumentation callbacks)
- Multi-transport C2 (HTTPS/DNS/ICMP) with AES-256-GCM tasking

Use Cases:
- Build a Windows implant that minimizes WinAPI telemetry and avoids common ntdll hook points
- Research/benchmark EDR detections against direct/indirect syscall execution and unhooking
- Test multiple injection primitives with polymorphic rotation to vary forensic artifacts
- Prototype covert C2 over DNS TXT or ICMP where HTTPS is restricted
- Validate syscall-number portability using SSN fingerprint export/import across hosts

Keywords:
Go, Plan9 assembly, direct syscalls, indirect syscalls, ntdll, PEB, LDR, PE export table parsing, SSN resolution, Hell’s Gate, syscall;ret gadget, unhooking, AMSI patch, ETW patch, NtTraceEvent, DbgUiRemoteBreakin, process injection, NtCreateSection, NtMapViewOfSection, NtCreateThreadEx, NtCreateUserProcess, NtQueueApcThread, DNS TXT C2, ICMP C2, HTTPS C2, AES-256-GCM, token impersonation, registry Run key persistence, NtQuerySystemInformation, VAD enumeration